---
import FeatureCard from '@chassis-ui/docs/components/FeatureCard.astro'
---

<section id="svg-section" class="home-section py-3xl md:py-6xl">
  <div class="container 2xl section-content">
    <div class="grid mb-3xl md:mb-6xl">
      <header class="section-header col-span-full lg:col-span-10 xl:col-span-8">
        <h2 id="svg">Working with SVGs</h2>

        <p>
          An SVG icon needs a few attributes in some browsers and with some screen readers. The
          markup of the examples above leaves them out, so add the ones that a project needs.
        </p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-md md:gap-xl">
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-shapes">
          <Fragment slot="title">Focus in Legacy Browsers</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            SVG elements receive keyboard focus by default in Internet Explorer and Edge Legacy. Add
            `focusable="false"` to prevent this behavior.
          </Fragment>
          <div class="border-top border-subtle pt-md mb-0">
            <a
              href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/18646111/disable-onfocus-event-for-svg-element"
              class="link-secondary"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              View solution on Stack Overflow →
            </a>
          </div>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>

      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-megaphone">
          <Fragment slot="title">Screen Reader Announcements</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            When using <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> elements with SVG sources, screen readers may skip
            the image or fail to announce it properly. Include <code>role="img"</code> on the
            element.
          </Fragment>
          <div class="border-top border-subtle pt-md mt-auto">
            <a
              href="https://web.archive.org/web/20201112013541/https://simplyaccessible.com/article/7-solutions-svgs/#acc-heading-2"
              class="link-secondary"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              Read accessibility guidance →
            </a>
          </div>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>

      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-thumbs-up">
          <Fragment slot="title">External Sprite Support (IE)</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            External SVG sprites using <code>&lt;use&gt;</code> with <code>href</code> attributes
            don't work in Internet Explorer. Apply the svg4everybody polyfill if IE support is
            required.
          </Fragment>
          <div class="border-top border-subtle pt-md mt-auto">
            <a
              href="https://github.com/jonathantneal/svg4everybody"
              class="link-secondary mb-0"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >
              View polyfill on GitHub →
            </a>
          </div>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
